# Architecture

## Split Layout

Frontend and backend are separate apps sharing a REST API at `/api/v1/`. Database schema lives in `db/migrations/`; backend wiring in `backend/cmd/api/main.go`.

## Backend Layers (`backend/internal/`)

```text
domain/         Pure business rules — no Echo, pgx, JSON/DB tags
application/    Use cases, port interfaces, DTOs, commands
delivery/http/  Echo handlers, middleware, HTTP request/response types
infrastructure/ Postgres repos, JWT, bcrypt, Viper config
platform/       Cross-cutting abstractions (clock, idgen)
```

**Dependency flow:** `delivery` → `application` → `domain`; `infrastructure` implements `application` interfaces.

## Frontend Layers (`frontend/src/`)

```text
pages/          Thin route views — compose composables + components
features/       auth, wod, workspace — each with api/, composables/, model/
shared/         httpClient, Base* form components, utilities
app/            App shell + router
styles/         Global CSS tokens (no component-scoped styles)
```

## Multi-Tenancy & Auth

- Authenticated requests: `Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>`
- Gym-scoped requests: also send `X-Gym-ID: <gymId>`
- RBAC enforced in both HTTP middleware and application services

## Extending the Domain

Follow `docs/EXTENDING_WOD_TYPES.md` — domain config interface → application DTOs → postgres mapper → HTTP handler → frontend schemas.
